  "details": "<p>Palaikastro is associated with the port of\u00a0Itanos and with the nearby Minoan site of Roussolakkos near the Chiona beach. The so-called Palaikastro Kouros, a chryselephantine statue of the fifteenth century B.C., was discovered at\u00a0<span>Palaikastro.</span></p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "Palaikastro, located in eastern Crete, was an important trading center in antiquity, from the Bronze Age going forward.",
